      "text": [
        ": سَأَلَهُ رَجُلٌ فَقَالَ أَصْلَحَكَ اَللَّهُ شُرْبُ اَلْخَمْرِ شَرٌّ أَمْ تَرْكُ اَلصَّلاَةِ قَالَ \"شُرْبُ اَلْخَمْرِ\" ثُمَّ قَالَ \"أَ وَ تَدْرِي لِمَ ذَلِكَ\" قَالَ لاَ قَالَ \"لِأَنَّهُ يَصِيرُ فِي حَالٍ لاَ يَعْرِفُ فِيهَا رَبَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4948 - Ibn Abi Umayr narrated from Isma'il ibn Salim, who reported from Abu Abdillah (as) that a man asked him:\n\"May Allah (swt) rectify you, is drinking alcohol worse or abandoning prayer?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"Drinking alcohol.\"\nThen Imam (as) said: \"Do you know why that is?\"\nThe man replied: \"No.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Because it leads a person to a state where he no longer recognizes his Lord (azj), the Mighty and Majestic.\""
        ]
      }
